<h2>Catechist's Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For class preparation and delivery. For the catechist's use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central theme:</strong> The Paschal Mystery of Christ is the heart of all the sacraments; in them his passage from death to life is made present.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand that the sacraments are actions of Christ, not human rites.</li>
<li>Know the seven sacraments and their relation to the Paschal Mystery.</li>
<li>Understand that the sacraments work <em>ex opere operato</em>.</li>
<li>Discover the indelible character of Baptism, Confirmation, and Holy Orders.</li>
<li>Value the connection between the Passover of Israel and the Christian sacraments.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key verse:</strong> <em>&laquo;We were buried therefore with him by baptism into death, so that as Christ was raised from the dead by the glory of the Father, we too might walk in newness of life&raquo;</em> (Rom 6:4)</p>
<p><strong>CCC references:</strong> 1135-1209, 1121, 1127-1129</p>

</section>

